cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Jacobian Monologue: Configuration-Gated Memory Delivery to a Language Model"
abstract: >-
  An experiment testing whether a relational configuration, composed in OpenUSD
  as a non-3D data layer, can gate whether a memory reaches a language model and
  thereby change the model's decision. A predicate over independently-authored
  facts wakes a dormant memory whose content contradicts the model's prior; the
  woken memory flips the model's forced-choice decision, and a one-relation
  counterfactual (holding all else identical) toggles the effect off. The result
  holds across multiple scenarios behind a pre-registered fairness gate. The
  memory reaches the model through the token stream, not by writing activations
  directly. A companion pre-registered experiment returns an honest null on a
  separate question (whether substrate ranking, rather than recency, drives
  workspace occupancy).
type: software
